@RULE WireWorld

Brian Silverman's WireWorld: electrons running along copper wire. State 0 is empty, 1 an electron's
head, 2 its tail, 3 copper.

@TABLE

# Written for automata from Golly's rule format (https://golly.sourceforge.io/Help/formats.html#rule),
# after the table in Golly's own Rules/WireWorld.rule: Moore, turned in eighths.

n_states:4
neighborhood:Moore
symmetries:rotate8

# Any state. Each is its own variable, because a variable written twice is the same state twice.
var a={0,1,2,3}
var b={0,1,2,3}
var c={0,1,2,3}
var d={0,1,2,3}
var e={0,1,2,3}
var f={0,1,2,3}
var g={0,1,2,3}
var h={0,1,2,3}

# Anything but a head.
var i={0,2,3}
var j={0,2,3}
var k={0,2,3}
var l={0,2,3}
var m={0,2,3}
var n={0,2,3}
var o={0,2,3}

# A head becomes a tail, and a tail becomes copper.
1,a,b,c,d,e,f,g,h,2
2,a,b,c,d,e,f,g,h,3

# Copper with exactly one head beside it becomes a head.
3,1,i,j,k,l,m,n,o,1

# Copper with exactly two: the second head one, two, three or four places on round the ring from the
# first, which with the turns covers every pair.
3,1,1,j,k,l,m,n,o,1
3,1,i,1,k,l,m,n,o,1
3,1,i,j,1,l,m,n,o,1
3,1,i,j,k,1,m,n,o,1

@COLORS

0 48 48 48     dark grey
1 0 128 255    head, light blue
2 255 255 255  tail, white
3 255 128 0    copper, orange
